<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><b>Risks
Related to Our Business and Industry</b></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><b><i>We
have a history of operating losses.</i></b></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.25in"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">Although
we recorded net loss in fiscal year 2026, we have recorded net profit in the previous fiscal year but losses in prior fiscal years
and may not maintain profitability in the future. Yatra&#8217;s net loss was INR 66.0 million for fiscal year 2026 as compared to a
profit of INR 23.5 million in fiscal year 2025 and a loss of INR 366.5 million in fiscal year 2024. If our revenues grow slower than
anticipated, or if our operating expenses exceed expectations, then we may not be able to achieve profitability in the near future
or at all, which may depress the price of our Ordinary Shares.</span></p>
<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.25in"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.25in"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><b><i>The
Indian travel industry is highly competitive, and we may not be able to effectively compete in the future.</i></b></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.25in"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">The
Indian travel industry is highly competitive. Our success depends upon our ability to compete effectively against numerous established
and emerging competitors, including other online travel agencies, or OTAs, traditional offline travel companies, travel research companies,
payment wallets, search engines, artificial intelligence chatbots and meta-search companies, both in India and abroad, such as Agoda
Company Pte. Ltd., Akbar Travels, Amazon India, Booking.com B.V., Cleartrip Pvt. Ltd., Expedia Southeast Asia Pte. Ltd., Flipkart Internet
Pvt. Ltd., Easy Trip Planners Limited, Thomas Cook India Limited, FCM Travel Solutions (India) Private Limited, GBT India Private Limited,
CWT India Private Limited, MakeMyTrip (India) Pvt. Ltd. (including Ibibo Group), One 97 Communications Limited, Oravel Stays Ltd., Riya
Travel and Tours (India) Private Limited, TBO Tek Limited, Happay Finance Ventures Private Limited Zaggle Prepaid Ocean Services Ltd
and Le Travenues Technology Limited, and in each case including their affiliated and group entities. Our competitors may have significantly
greater personnel resources, financial resources, marketing resources and other resources than we have. Factors affecting our competitive
success include price, availability of travel products, ability to package travel products across multiple suppliers, brand recognition,
customer service and customer care, fees charged to customers, ease of use, accessibility, reliability, and innovation. If we are not
able to compete effectively against our competitors, our business and results of operations and cash flows may be adversely affected.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.25in"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.25in"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">We
face increasing competition from large, established internet search engines with a global presence, particularly Google, as well as
from artificial intelligence chatbots and meta-search companies that aggregate travel search results. These search engines have
grown in popularity and may offer comprehensive travel planning, shopping, and booking capabilities, potentially directing more
traffic to the websites of our suppliers, competitors, or their own travel-related offerings. Some competitors have also launched
brand marketing campaigns to enhance their visibility with customers and possess significantly greater personnel, financial,
marketing, and other resources than we do, as well as longer operating histories and stronger reputations in the Indian travel
market. In addition, meta-search sites such as TripAdvisor Inc., Trivago NV, Skyscanner, and Kayak enable users to make reservations
directly on their platforms, which may reduce the traffic and transactions directed to us through referrals. If more meta-search
sites introduce direct-booking capabilities or if search engines further expand their travel products and services, our ability to
attract traffic to our websites and secure prominent placement in paid or organic search results at a reasonable cost, or at all,
could be adversely affected. As a result of these competitive pressures, we have periodically reduced, and may need to reduce in the
future, our service fees and Adjusted Margin % to remain competitive and maintain or increase our market share.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.25in"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.25in"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">We
may face increased competition from new entrants in our industry. The travel industry is extremely dynamic and new channels of distribution
in the travel industry may negatively affect our market share. Additional sources of competition include large companies that offer online
travel services as one part of their business model, such as Alibaba Group Holding Ltd, as well as &#8220;daily deal&#8221; websites,
such as Groupon, Inc.&#8217;s Getaways, or peer-to-peer inventory sources, such as Airbnb Inc., VRBO.com and Oravel Stays Ltd., which
provide home and apartment rentals as an alternative to hotel rooms. Recently, the growth of peer-to-peer inventory sources has affected
the demand for our services in facilitating reservations at hotels, particularly in overseas markets. We cannot assure that we will be
able to successfully compete against existing or new competitors in our existing lines of business as well as new lines of business into
which we may venture. If we fail to compete effectively, our business, cash flows, and results of operations may be adversely affected.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.25in"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>


