<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><span style="text-decoration: underline">Service
Tax refund Claim.</span></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">Refund
claim of INR 3.91 million was filed in June 2018 and in response to the refund claim, a deficiency memo was issued by Assistant Commissioner,
GST, Gurugram on August 8, 2018, asking for certain information. Yatra Online submitted some information vide reply dated January 23,
2019.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">However,
refund claim was rejected on the grounds of non-submission of information within a reasonable time from the date of issuance of deficiency
memo. This rejection order was not received by Yatra Online and only after multiple follow ups Yatra Online was provided with the copy
of it in September 2020.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">Accordingly,
appeal was filed before Commissioner (Appeals) on November 02, 2020, and personal hearing was granted on December 09, 2020. Yatra Online
submitted the additional information sought by the officer pursuant to such hearing.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">The
Commissioner (Appeals) via an order dated February 12, 2021, has remanded back the matter for verification. Yatra Online through its
authorized representatives subsequently approached the original authority for verification process. There has been no further update
on this matter.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><span style="text-decoration: underline">Goods
and Services Tax Audit Demand Order-Fiscal Year 2019-20</span></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">For
the fiscal year 2019-20, Yatra Online Limited underwent a Departmental GST Audit under Section 65 by the Haryana Tax Department, initiated via
Form ADT-01 on January 11, 2024. Following the audit report issued on May 28, 2024, and multiple personal hearings through March 2026
where reconciliation for ITC claims and vehicle sales was provided, the department issued an adverse order on March 30, 2026, creating
a total demand of 36.4 million (including interest and penalty). Maintaining strong merits regarding legitimate credit reversals and
vehicle sale loss calculations, the company has been filed an official appeal on 28 Jun 2026 and has categorized the 36.4 million demand
as a contingent liability.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><span style="text-decoration: underline">Goods
and Services Tax Show Cause and Demand Notice -Fiscal Year 2019-20</span></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">For
the fiscal year 2019-20, Yatra Online Limited received an adverse demand order of 0.52 million from the Haryana GST Department under Section 16(2)(c)
seeking recovery of Input Tax Credit due to non-payment of output tax by a vendor, Starcrest Service Private Limited. The company appealed
against the demand order. The appellate order upheld the demand with the assurance that the amount would be refunded once the department
recovers tax from the vendor. To prevent ongoing exposure, the company paid 0.52 million under protest via Form DRC-03 on March 22, 2025,
and successfully secured departmental approval in September 2025 for an interest and penalty waiver, classifying the 0.52 million as
a contingent liability.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><span style="text-decoration: underline">Goods
and Services Tax Show Cause and Notice -Fiscal Year 2020-21</span></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">For
the fiscal year 2020-21, Yatra Online Limited received an ASMT-10 notice on October 15, 2024, from the Haryana GST Department,
followed by Form DRC-01 proposing a demand of 119 million across multiple return discrepancies. After detailed reconciliations were
filed, the department issued an order under Section 73 on February 27, 2025, substantially reducing the demand to 2.26 million (tax
of 1.16 million, interest of 0.94 million, and penalty of 0.16 million). The company accepted the demand of Rs. 0.15 million and
appealed in the appellate forum for the rest amount on May-25. The remaining amount has been categorized under the contingent.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>


