<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><span style="text-decoration: underline">Goods
and Services Tax Show Cause and Demand Order-Fiscal Year 2021-22</span></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">For
the fiscal year 2021-22, Yatra Online Limited received a DRC-01A notice on June 19, 2025, followed by a Show Cause Notice on
September 4, 2025, from the Gujarat GST Department regarding output tax, late fees, and ineligible credit on motor vehicles and
catering. The company paid accepted liabilities totaling 0.041 Million (comprising output tax, interest, and late fees) via Form
DRC-03 on July 24, 2025, and submitted replies contesting the remaining issues. After the department passed an adverse order on
March 12, 2026, demanding 3.76 million for hotel accommodation services credit, the company filed an official appeal on March 12,
2026 in the appellate forum, and classified the 3.76 million demand as a contingent liability.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><span style="text-decoration: underline">Goods
and Service Tax Show Cause and Demand Notice-Fiscal Year 2018-19</span></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">Yatra
Online Limited received a DRC-01 notice from the Department of Goods and Service Tax (Gov. of Haryana) on June 24, 2025, concerning an input tax
credit (ITC) transfer of 0.01 million passed on to Cemex Pharma, which was flagged as a non-existent firm for the fiscal year 2018-19.
The company filed a formal reply on July 7, 2025, along with a DRC-03 submission. A penalty liability of 0.0069 was fully settled,
leading management to classify the final resolution of this matter as probable to be dropped. Awaiting for the final order.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><span style="text-decoration: underline">Goods
and Service Tax Show Cause and Demand Notice-Fiscal Year 2024-25</span></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">The
Department of Goods and Service Tax in Uttar Pradesh issued an ASMT-10 clarification notice to Yatra Online Limited regarding an alleged excess
claim of input tax credit amounting to 1.26 million. The company submitted its comprehensive reply on April 28, 2025, explaining that
the highlighted ITC mismatch was due to credits legitimately claimed in February 2025 for the operational period spanning April to October
2024. Backed by valid documentation, the company assesses the risk of any sustained demand as remote. Further no communication received from department.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><span style="text-decoration: underline">Goods
and Service Tax Show Cause and Demand Notice-Fiscal Year 2021-22</span></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">For
the fiscal year 2021-22, Yatra Online Limited faced a multi-stage dispute in Karnataka that began with an offline ASMT-10 notice, moved to an
online DRC-01A, and culminated in a Show Cause Notice (SCN) issued on September 30, 2025, involving an ITC discrepancy of 1.65 million.
Although the company provided detailed evidence showing the credit was accounted for via a net-effect adjustment in the subsequent fiscal
period, the department issued an adverse tax demand order in December 2025. The company subsequently filed an official appeal on March
25, 2026 in appellate forum, and has recorded the 1.65 million demand as a contingent liability.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><span style="text-decoration: underline">Goods
and Service Tax Show Cause and Demand Notice-Fiscal Year 2025-26</span></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">Yatra
Online Limited received an ASMT-10 notice from the Uttar Pradesh GST authorities on August 19, 2025, concerning an alleged excess input tax credit
claim of 0.1 million stemming from a GSTR-3B vs GSTR-2A mismatch for June 2025. A detailed response was filed on September 8, 2025, demonstrating
that the disputed credit belonged to a previous period and was validly brought forward to the current period. The company is currently
awaiting final drop orders from the Adjudicating Authority department, maintaining a remote risk classification.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><span style="text-decoration: underline">Goods
and Service Tax Show Cause and Demand Notice-Fiscal Year 2021-22</span></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">The
Department of Goods and Service Tax in Bihar issued an offline SCN on September 4, 2025, to Yatra Online Limited regarding an excess ITC claim
of 0.55 million for the 2021-22 financial year. The company submitted its rebuttal via email and physical channels on September 11, 2025,
clarifying that the credit belonged to an earlier period and was fully legitimate. Because the statutory due date for the proper officer
to pass an adjudication order has officially lapsed without further administrative action, the matter is categorized as remote.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><span style="text-decoration: underline">Goods
and Service Tax Show Cause and Demand Notice-Fiscal Year 2025-26</span></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">An
ASMT-10 notice was served to Yatra Online Limited by the Uttar Pradesh GST department on September 9, 2025 for the period July-2025, raising inquiries
over an excess ITC claim of 0.24 million. The company submitted a formal reply on September 30, 2025, providing a clear audit trail of
the underlying transactions. Based on the legitimacy of the submissions, the company anticipates that the notice will be dropped upon
final review, rendering the financial risk remote.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><span style="text-decoration: underline">Goods
and Service Tax Show Cause and Demand Notice-Fiscal Year 2021-22</span></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">In
Assam, Yatra Online Limited received a DRC-01 SCN on September 29, 2025, concerning a 1 million variance in short-paid output liability and excess
ITC for the 2021-22 fiscal year. The company filed its reply on October 31, 2025, followed by the submission of additional clarifying
data on December 29, 2025, after attending three personal hearings. As the statutory limitation period for the department to issue a
final order has since expired without communication, the matter is classified under remote risk.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>


