<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><span style="text-decoration: underline">Goods
and Service Tax Show Cause and Demand Notice-Fiscal Year 2024-25</span></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">The
Uttar Pradesh GST Adjudicating authorities issued a DRC-01A notice under Section 74 to Yatra Online Limited on October 16, 2025, demanding
28.68 million due to an alleged excess claim of ITC and output discrepancies arising from a field officer reporting the principal
place of business as non-existent. The company filed a robust response on October 30, 2025, enclosing the formal physical
verification survey report and a valid rent agreement to substantiate the active existence of their premises. The company maintains
that the notice will be dropped, classifying the risk as remote.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><span style="text-decoration: underline">Goods
and Service Tax Show Cause and Demand Notice-Fiscal Year 2025-26</span></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">Yatra
Online Limited was served an ASMT-10 notice for the period August-2025 on October 27, 2025, by the Uttar Pradesh tax department regarding an excess
input tax credit claim of 0.23 million in August 2025. The company submitted its reply on November 9, 2025, proving that the credit belonged
to the preceding fiscal year (2024-25) and was legally claimed within permitted statutory timelines. Consequently, the company has treated
the potential exposure from this notice as remote.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><span style="text-decoration: underline">Goods
and Service Tax Show Cause and Demand Notice-Fiscal Years 2024-25 and 2025-26</span></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">An
offline SCN was issued to Yatra Online Limited by the Delhi GST department on October 28, 2025, alleging a cash shortfall in output liability
payments amounting to 2.37 million across the 2024-25 and 2025-26 periods. The company submitted its physical representation to the department
on December 18, 2025, detailing that the reduction in cash outlays was the direct result of adjusting valid, legally available portal
ITC balances. Given that these adjustments conform fully to the law, the probability of an adverse outcome is classified as remote.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><span style="text-decoration: underline">Goods
and Service Tax Show Cause and Demand Notice-Fiscal Year 2025-26</span></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">The
Uttar Pradesh GST authority served an ASMT-10 notice to Yatra Online Limited on December 9, 2025, contesting an excess ITC claim of 2.84 million
(split equally at Rs.1.42 million each for CGST and SGST) during September 2025. The company&#8217;s reply outlined that the credit originated
from a previous period and was correctly brought forward into the current month&#8217;s return. Backed by verified transaction ledgers,
the matter is classified as a remote exposure.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><span style="text-decoration: underline">Goods
and Service Tax Show Cause and Demand Notice -Fiscal Year 2020-21</span></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">For
the financial year 2020-21, Yatra Online Limited received a notice under form DRC-01A (Section 74) from the Department of Goods and Service Tax,
Madhya Pradesh (Adjudicating Authority). The notice demanded clarification regarding an excess Input Tax Credit (ITC) claim identified
through a comparison of GSTR-2A with GSTR-3B, amounting to 0.69 million. A formal reply was submitted on June 17, 2025. Following the
submission, the matter was closed with a nil demand in July-2025, and the notice has been officially dropped.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><span style="text-decoration: underline">Goods
and Service Tax Show Cause and Demand Notice -Fiscal Year 2022-23</span></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">For
the financial year 2022-23, Yatra Online Limited was served a DRC-01A notice by the Department of Goods and Service Tax, Madhya
Pradesh. The notice called for clarification regarding an excess ITC claim arising from GSTR-2A and GSTR-3B discrepancies, totaling
0.29 million. The company filed its reply on June 17, 2025. The Adjudicating Authority subsequently dropped the notice in July-2025, closing the
matter with a nil demand.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><span style="text-decoration: underline">Goods
and Service Tax Show Cause and Demand Notice -Fiscal Year 2021-22</span></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">For
the financial year 2021-22, Yatra Online Limited received an ASMT-10 notice on July 15, 2025, from the Department of Goods and Service Tax, Maharashtra.
The notice demanded clarification for a sum of 5.83 million due to short-paid outward liability, input liability, and ineligible ITC
involving cancelled dealers. The company filed its reply on August 15, 2025, leading to the notice being entirely dropped with a nil
demand on September 27, 2025.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><span style="text-decoration: underline">Goods
and Service Tax Show Cause Notice-Fiscal Year 2021-22</span></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">For
the financial year 2021-22, Yatra Online Limited received a Show Cause Notice dated December 31, 2022, from the Department of Goods and
Service Tax, Odisha. The department raised a demand of 0.60 million based on excess ITC claimed in GSTR-3B compared to GSTR-2A. The
company submitted its reply and the requested documents on May 22, 2024. Following a personal hearing, the SCN was successfully
dropped with a nil demand 10 Oct 2025.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>


