<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><span style="text-decoration: underline">Goods
and Service Tax Show Cause and Demand Notice -Fiscal Year 2021-22</span></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">For
the financial year 2021-22, Yatra Online Limited was served a DRC-01A notice on April 30, 2025, by the Department of Goods and Service Tax, Tamil
Nadu. The notice flagged excess ITC claims, ineligible ITC, interest in late invoice reporting in GSTR-1, and late fees, totaling 1.06
million. A reply was submitted on May 15, 2025, clarifying that the ITC difference belonged to the prior period. The department later
escalated the matter to a Show Cause Notice under DRC-01 on June 25, 2025. The company accepted and paid a minor late fee and interest
portion of 0.01 million via DRC-03 on August 6, 2025, while contesting the remainder. Following additional document submissions was made in 06 Aug 2025,
the Adjudicating Authority passed an order in December 2025 dropping the entire demand.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><span style="text-decoration: underline">Goods
and Service Tax Show Cause and Demand Notice -Fiscal Year 2021-22</span></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">For
the financial year 2021-22, Yatra Online Limited received a DRC-01 notice on June 30, 2025, from the Department of Goods and Service
Tax, Delhi. The authority demanded a clarification for 1.34 million based on short-paid outward liability, input liability, and
ineligible ITC related to motor vehicles. The company filed a merit-based reply on July 21, 2025, proving that liability had already
been settled and the ITC belonged to prior fiscal years. Following the submission of documents and a personal hearing, the final
order was issued with a nil demand in 7 Nov 2025.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><span style="text-decoration: underline">Goods
and Service Tax Show Cause Notice-Fiscal Year 2021-22</span></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">For
the financial year 2021-22, Yatra Online Limited issued an ASMT-10 notice in August 2025 by the Department of Goods and Service Tax,
Uttar Pradesh due to output tax variances between GSTR-3B and GSTR-1, and ITC differences between GSTR-3B and GSTR-2A. A reply was
submitted on September 8, 2025. The department subsequently dropped several items and issued a DRC-01 notice on September 22, 2025,
narrowing the dispute down to a 0.04 million demand covering output tax, creditors beyond 180 days, expenses ITC, and other income.
The base demand of 0.02 million was paid, and the department issued a final order imposing a penalty of 0.02 million, which has been
paid to close the matter in 03-Dec-2025.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><span style="text-decoration: underline">Goods
and Service Tax Show Cause Notice-Fiscal Year 2021-22</span></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">For
the financial year 2021-22, Yatra Online Limited received an ASMT-10 notice on August 20, 2025, from the Department of Goods and Service Tax,
Tamil Nadu demanding 0.96 million due to missing details on credit notes and nil-rated supplies. The company filed an immediate reply
on August 20, 2025. The department subsequently issued a Show Cause Notice on September 24, 2025. An online response was submitted on
October 27, 2025, and following active communication and clarification with the officer, the entire demand was dropped via an order issued
in December 2025.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><span style="text-decoration: underline">Goods
and Service Tax Show Cause Notice-Fiscal Year 2021-22</span></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">For
the financial year 2021-22, Yatra Online Limited received a DRC-01 Show Cause Notice on September 30, 2025, from the Department of
Goods and Service Tax, Government of Telangana. The authority alleged an excess ITC claim (1.48 million) and ineligible ITC (1.0
million) under Section 17(5) amounting to 2.48 million. The company filed its defense on October 30, 2025. Following communication
and verification of the submitted proof, the officer passed an order with a nil demand, dropping all charges in Nov 2025.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>


