<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 10pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -10pt"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><span style="text-decoration: underline">Service
Tax Show Cause and Demand Notice-Fiscal Years 2007-11</span></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 10pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -10pt"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.25in"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">In
August 2011, following an audit by the service tax authorities, we were issued a notice pertaining to certain travel industry matters
from fiscal years 2007-11, which involve a nuanced interpretation of Indian law. We responded to this in April 2012 and made an additional
submission in July 2014. Subsequent to these proceedings, the Commissioner of Service Tax levied a demand for INR 237.6 million in service
tax, accompanied by an equal penalty and additional interest at a specified rate. In response, we lodged an appeal against this order
with the Customs, Excise, and Service Tax Appellate Tribunal (&#8220;CESTAT&#8221;) in January 2017.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.25in"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">Early
Hearing petition was heard on April 5, 2024, and the matter was listed for final hearing on April 29, 2024</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">The
case was subsequently adjourned to June 10, 2024, due to ongoing election.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">On
June 10, 2024, the hearing date was scheduled and on July 18, 2024, the order was pronounced, receiving the final order in the favor
of the company.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.25in"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">We
filed the refund application for the pre-deposit amount of INR 17.82m. On July 10, 2025, the company received the refund order of INR
17.82 million along with applicable interest of INR 9.06 million. On 21.08.2025 we received a refund against the pre-deposit of INR 26.88
million (including interest)</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><span style="text-decoration: underline">Goods
and Service Tax Show Cause and Demand Notice-Fiscal Year 2022-23</span></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">Yatra
TG Stays Private Limited received an ASMT-10 notice from the Karnataka GST adjudicating department on October 28, 2025, regarding a
short payment of output liability totaling 1.6 million. Upon internal reconciliation, the company accepted a minor tax shortfall of
0.02 million, which promptly settled along with interest through Form DRC-03 on November 14, 2025. The remaining contested balance
of 0.13 million is considered legally defensible. A reply was filed on November 11, 2025 and has been classified as remote. No further communication received from department.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><span style="text-decoration: underline">Goods
and Service Tax Show Cause and Demand Notice-Fiscal Year 2023-24</span></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">Yatra
TG Stays Private Limited received an ASMT-10 notice on January 9, 2026, from the Puducherry GST department regarding an output liability
variance of 0.2 million. The company filed a clarification on January 23, 2026, showing that the discrepancy was purely an artifact of
a reporting format adjustment for Section 9(5) e-commerce platform supplies handled for unregistered entities. The case holds a remote
risk classification as no tax evasion took place. No further communication received from department.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><span style="text-decoration: underline">Goods
and Service Tax Show Cause and Demand Notice-Fiscal Year 2022-23</span></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">The
Puducherry GST department issued an ASMT-10 notice on January 9, 2026, to Yatra TG Stays Private Limited concerning an output liability
difference of 0.2 million for FY 2022-23. The company filed its reply on January 23, 2026, explaining that the reporting variance occurred
when Section 9(5) supplies were legally transitioned from the standard B2C tables to Table 3.1.1 from July 2022 onward. The matter is
expected to be closed without any demand, maintaining a remote status. No further communication received from department.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><span style="text-decoration: underline">Goods
and Service Tax Show Cause and Demand Notice-Fiscal Year 2023-24</span></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">Yatra
TG Stays Private Limited was served an ASMT-10 notice by the Maharashtra GST authorities on January 13, 2026, highlighting a 0.25 million
discrepancy linked to output liabilities and ITC from cancelled suppliers. A formal defense was submitted on February 13, 2026, proving
that the discrepancy was caused by an amendment in Form GSTR-1 and that the transactions involved place-of-supply rules outside of Maharashtra,
meaning no local ITC was ever claimed. The company has classified the matter as remote. No further communication received from department.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>


