<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><span style="text-decoration: underline">Goods
and Service Tax Audit Notice-Fiscal Year 2022-23</span></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">The
Maharashtra GST department initiated a statutory audit under Section 65 for the fiscal year 2022-23 against Yatra TG Stays Private Limited,
issuing a notice on January 5, 2026, to request full financial ledgers and tax return summaries. The company successfully compiled and
shared its primary documents with the audit officer on January 30, 2026. The company submitted the required documents to Adjudicating Authority on 21 May 2026, the company anticipates smooth closure, keeping the risk classification remote.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><span style="text-decoration: underline">Goods
and Service Tax Show Cause and Demand Notice -Fiscal Year 2021-22</span></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">For
the financial year 2021-22, Yatra TG Stays Private Limited received a DRC-01A notice from the Department of Goods and Service Tax, Madhya
Pradesh. The case pertained to a short payment of output liability identified in a GSTR-1 vs GSTR-3B comparison, carrying a tax impact
of 0.01 million. The company accepted the demand of 0.005 million, which was subsequently paid along with a self-calculated interest
of 0.002 million each under CGST and SGST (totaling 0.008 million) via DRC-03 on July 28, 2025. A formal reply was filed on the same
day, and the notice was officially closed and dropped with a nil remaining demand on October 9, 2025.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><span style="text-decoration: underline">Goods
and Service Tax Show Cause and Demand Notice -Fiscal Year 2022-23</span></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">For
the financial year 2022-23, Yatra TG Stays Private Limited was issued a DRC-01A notice by the Department of Goods and Service Tax, Madhya
Pradesh. The notice requested clarification on a short payment of output liability from a GSTR-1 and GSTR-3B reconciliation, totaling
0.04 million. A response was submitted on June 19, 2025, and after reviewing the clarification, the authority dropped the notice with
a nil demand on October 9, 2025.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><span style="text-decoration: underline">Goods
and Service Show Cause and Demand Notice -Fiscal Year 2023-24</span></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">For
the financial year 2023-24, Yatra TG Stays Private Limited faced a DRC-01A notice from the Department of Goods and Service Tax, Madhya
Pradesh. The dispute related to a short payment of output liability based on GSTR-1 vs GSTR-3B discrepancies, amounting to 0.07 million.
The company filed its reply on June 19, 2025, resulting in the notice being successfully dropped with a nil demand on October 9, 2025.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><span style="text-decoration: underline">Goods
and Service Tax TCS Audit Notice-Fiscal Year 2021-22 to 2024-25</span></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">For
the multi-year block spanning FY 2021-22 to FY 2024-25 (with the audit spanning data from FY 2020-21 to FY 2023-24), Yatra TG Stays Private
Limited issued an audit notice on December 18, 2025, by the Dehradun Audit Circle-1, Uttarakhand. The department initiated an audit concerning
TCS details, profit &amp; loss accounts, audit reports, ITRs, and return commissions. The company progressively submitted the required
details on December 24, December 29, January 2, January 6, and January 8, 2026. The department has requested further detailed reports
regarding cancelled dealers and late fee confirmations, Company submitted the requisite documents in Feb&#8217;26 &amp;
the matter has been dropped in Mar&#8217;26.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><b><i>Tax
Matters Relating to Yatra Hotel Solutions Private Limited (formerly known as Desiya Online Travel Distribution Pvt. Ltd.)</i></b></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 10pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -10pt"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><span style="text-decoration: underline">Service
Tax Show Cause and Demand Notice-October 2012 to October 2013</span></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 10pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -10pt"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.25in"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">In
January 2014, we submitted a refund claim application to the service tax authorities for INR 8.5 million. However, in March 2014, the
service tax department sent a notice rejecting our refund claim. We responded to the Assistant Commissioner of Service Tax in July 2014.
Subsequent requests for documentation and clarification were made by the Office of the Assistant Commissioner in February and March 2015,
to which we complied in February 2016 and followed up with a letter in June 2018.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 26pt"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.25in"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">On
December 3, 2018, the Assistant Commissioner of Central Tax in Kolkata instructed the Deputy/Assistant Commissioner of Central Tax in
Mumbai to verify the interest paid on advances. Following a meeting on January 8, 2019, we provided the required submissions by January
28, 2019. After sending a follow-up letter to the Kolkata authorities on September 30, 2019, they requested additional details on October
30, 2019. We promptly addressed this request on November 19, 2019.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 26pt"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>


<!-- Field: Page; Sequence: 79; Value: 1 -->
    <div style="border-bottom: Black 1pt solid; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 6pt"><table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; font-size: 10pt"><tr style="vertical-align: top; text-align: left"><td style="text-align: center; width: 100%"><!-- Field: Sequence; Type: Arabic; Name: PageNo -->77<!-- Field: /Sequence --></td></tr></table></div>
    <div style="break-before: page; margin-top: 6pt; margin-bottom: 0pt"><table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; font-size: 10pt"><tr style="vertical-align: top; text-align: left"><td style="width: 100%"><a href="#Toc_001">Table of Contents</a></td></tr></table></div>
    <!-- Field: /Page -->

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.25in"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">By
March 2021, we were granted a refund of INR 7.4 million, with the remaining INR 1.1 million being denied due to time limitations. This
refunded amount was credited to our bank account.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.25in"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">For
the rejected INR 1.1 million and its interest component, we lodged an appeal with the Kolkata Commissioner (Appeals) on July 26, 2021.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.25in"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">Department
has filed an appeal sanctioned refund amount of INR 73.87 million on the grounds that it is not substantiated that service tax refund
is not hit by unjust enrichment. Further, it is not clear whether the service tax liability was pertaining to Kolkata service tax registration
or Mumbai service tax registration and few other re-conciliation issues between financials and service tax return. In our view, to filing
the appeal, the department has gone beyond the SCN and has raised grounds which were not raised at original adjudication stage. Further,
documents submitted on record have not been considered while filing an appeal. The company is in the process of filing a reply and would do the same before hearing on May 15, 2024. A favorable order in the above matter
of INR 73.87 million has been received in this case.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><span style="text-decoration: underline">Goods
and Services Tax Show Cause and Demand Notice -Fiscal Year 2020-21</span></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">For
the fiscal year 2020-21, Yatra Hotel Solutions Private Limited (Desiya) received a notice on November 29, 2024, from the Maharashtra
GST Department regarding excess Input Tax Credit claims. The company submitted responses and attended personal hearings on February
21, 2025, showing that the credit pertained to FY 2019-20 claimed in FY 2020-21; nevertheless, the department issued a demand order
on February 27, 2025, totaling 1.22 million (tax of 0.61 million, interest of 0.54 million, and penalty of 0.06 million). The
company subsequently filed an official appeal in May 2025 at appellate authority and has recorded the 1.22 million demand as a
contingent liability.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><span style="text-decoration: underline">Goods
and Services Tax Summon-Fiscal Years 2018-19 to 2022-23</span></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">For
the fiscal years 2018-19 through 2022-23, Yatra Hotel Solutions Private Limited (Desiya) received an offline summon notice from the DGGI
Zonal Unit, Gurugram and Maharashtra GST Department requesting clarification on Input Tax Credit availment across multiple years. The
company submitted written requests for adjournment on December 16, 2024, and May 30, 2025, clarifying that the credit discrepancies related
to prior periods. Pending further official communication or formal demand from the authority, the company maintains that the matter will
be dropped as company submitted the documents in Mar&#8217;26 and considers the financial risk remote.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><span style="text-decoration: underline">Goods
and Services Tax Show Cause and Demand Notice - Fiscal Year 2021-22</span></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">For
the fiscal year 2021-22, Yatra Hotel Solutions Private Limited (Desiya) faced an Input Tax Credit dispute in Maharashtra originating
from Form ASMT-10 issued on February 10, 2025, which culminated in a Show Cause Notice and an adverse demand order in Form DRC-07 issued
in December 2025 for 3.66 million. Although the company provided detailed evidence and attended personal hearings showing that the credit
related to prior-year intercompany transactions validly claimed under Section 16(2), the officer sustained the demand. The company filed
an official appeal before the Commissioner (Appeals) on March 30, 2026, and has recorded the 36.62 lakhs demand as a contingent liability.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><span style="text-decoration: underline">Goods
and Service Tax Show Cause and Demand Notice -Fiscal Year 2021-22 to 2024-25</span></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">Covering
the multi-year period from FY 2021-22 to FY 2024-25, Yatra Hotel Solutions Private Limited (Desiya) received a DRC-01 Show Cause Notice
and subsequent reminder from the Department of Goods and Service Tax, Andhra Pradesh on September 27, 2025, and October 31, 2025. The
matter involved a short payment of output liability totaling 0.03 million excluding interest. The company requested an adjournment to
file its response on November 12, 2025. Ultimately, an order was passed raising a final demand of 0.04 million, which the company paid
in full via DRC-03 to close the matter.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.25in"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>


<!-- Field: Page; Sequence: 80; Value: 1 -->
    <div style="border-bottom: Black 1pt solid; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 6pt"><table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; font-size: 10pt"><tr style="vertical-align: top; text-align: left"><td style="text-align: center; width: 100%"><!-- Field: Sequence; Type: Arabic; Name: PageNo -->78<!-- Field: /Sequence --></td></tr></table></div>
