<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><b><i>Tax
Matters Relating to TSI Yatra Private Limited</i></b></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.25in"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 10pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -10pt"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><span style="text-decoration: underline">Assessment
Year 2016-17</span></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 10pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -10pt"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.25in"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">In
September 2017, Indian income tax authorities issued us a notice regarding tax deduction at source for the assessment year 2016-17, requesting
specific details by September 27, 2017. We promptly complied and submitted the necessary information.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.25in"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">The
following month, in October 2017, the tax authorities sent another notice pertaining to the 2016-17 assessment year. This notice imposed
a penalty of INR 0.76 million for our failure to withhold taxes. A hearing was scheduled for October 24, 2017, during which we were instructed
to provide additional information. We furnished the requested details and have not heard back from the authorities since then.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.25in"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><span style="text-decoration: underline">Assessment
Year 2018-19</span></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 10pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -10pt"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.25in"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">In
March 2021, the Income Tax Authorities issued us a notice under section 142(1) requesting details and clarification on a &#8220;share
based payment expense&#8221; totaling INR 9.3 million. We promptly provided the requested response.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 26pt"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.25in"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">Subsequently,
in April 2021, the authorities passed an order under section 143(3), disallowing this expense. As a result, we faced a tax and penalty
imposition totaling approximately INR 0.4 million, accompanied by a demand notice under section 156 and a show-cause notice under section
270A. In response, we filed an appeal with the Commissioner of Income Tax (Appeal) on May 12, 2021.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.25in"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">On
October 9, 2024, we received notice from CIT(A) against which the reply was filed on October 16, 2024.. We submitted the reply to the
Commissioner of Income Tax (Appeal), Delhi, on October 16, 2024, in response to the notice issued on October 9, 2024. Subsequently, the
company received order u/s 250 dated January 3, 2025, which was not in our favor. We have filed an appeal with ITAT against the said
order on March 04, 2025 which is yet to be disposed off and the matter is being heard.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><span style="text-decoration: underline">Assessment
Year 2016-17</span></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">An
order under section 201/201(1A) dated March 31, 2022 was passed, regarding the delay in furnishing the TDS certificate in form 16/16A
within the time limit raising a demand of 1.31 million. The department initiated the proceedings under section 272A(2)(g). On March 27,
2023, the department issued the penalty order in continuation to the above proceeding under section 272A(2)(g). Against the above order,
TSI filed the reply on November 1, 2023. However, the response made by TSI was not acceptable to the department.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">The
appeal against the order was submitted to CIT(A), though after the due date, accompanied by a condonation application for the delay.On
9.12.2025 complete submission was made to CIT(A) and we are awaiting the final order.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><span style="text-decoration: underline">Assessment
Year 2022-23</span></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">The
Company filed its income tax return for AY 2022-23 by declaring an income of 30.00 million. The return of income was processed u/s 154
read with section 143(1) of the Act at an income of 83.42 million with a demand of 16.42 million. Subsequently, the income tax assessment
unit completed the proceedings &amp; passed order under section 143(3) read with section 144B of the Act, at an assessed income of 179.2
million and raised a demand of 47.78 million.. Prima facie, the authorities while making the above addition, have compared the closing
ledger balances with the information reported in Company&#8217;s AIS report i.e. the amount of transactions in the financial year 2021-22
as reported by the suppliers has been compared with the closing balance as outstanding their ledger accounts. This mechanism adopted
by the income tax authorities is incorrect at the first place itself and that the addition made pursuant to the same are liable to be
deleted. Being aggrieved with the impugned order, the Company filed appeal on 20 April 2024 Detailed reply with Indian Tax Authorities
CIT(A) was additionally filed on May 19, 2025. Final order from CIT(A) is awaited.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>


