<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 10pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -10pt"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><span style="text-decoration: underline">Service
Tax Show Cause and Demand Notice-Fiscal Years 2007-12</span></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 10pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -10pt"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.25in"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">In
October 2013, following an audit by the service tax authorities, we received a notice pertaining to fiscal years 2007-12. This notice
addressed specific issues related to the travel industry and required nuanced interpretations of Indian law. Responding to this, we submitted
a reply to the Commissioner of Service Tax in March 2014. Subsequent to these discussions, the Commissioner levied a service tax demand
of INR 19.94 million, coupled with an equal penalty and interest calculated at the prevailing rate. In December 2016, we challenged this
order at the Customs, Excise and Service Tax Appellate Tribunal (CESTAT) and made a preliminary payment equivalent to 7.5% of the demanded
duty.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.25in"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.25in"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">The
appeals were allowed by the CESTAT Chandigarh by way of Final Order dated for the years starting 2007-12 30.03.2026. We have
received the refund order dated 16.07.2026 against the pre-deposit of INR 1.96 million (including interest).</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 10pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -10pt"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><span style="text-decoration: underline">Service
Tax Show Cause and Demand Notice-Fiscal Years 2010-14</span></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 10pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -10pt"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.25in"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">In
October 2015, we were notified by the service tax authorities regarding issues from fiscal years 2010-14, specifically concerning the
travel industry and its intricate interpretations under Indian law. We addressed this by submitting our response to the Commissioner
of Service Tax in March 2016 and subsequently attended a personal hearing before the Commissioner of Central Excise. The total demand
stemming from this notice approximates INR 231.6 million, exclusive of any potential interest and penalties. On January 13, 2017, we
participated in another hearing before the Additional Director General and presented an additional submission to the adjudicating authority
by January 27, 2017.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 26pt"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.25in"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">Following
these discussions, the Directorate General of GST Intelligence formalized a service tax demand of INR 231.6 million, in addition to the
applicable interest. To contest this order, we approached the Customs, Excise and Service Tax Appellate Tribunal (CESTAT) in November
2017, accompanied by a 7.5% pre-deposit of the total duty as mandated by service tax regulations.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 26pt"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.25in"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">Our
request for an expedited hearing was approved by CESTAT on May 20, 2019, at the behest of the department, setting the stage for a conclusive
discussion. However, the scheduled hearing for August 9, 2019 was postponed. While the CESTAT Chandigarh bench planned to convene in
January 2020, the agenda remained unreleased to the public and the hearing could not take place.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.25in"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">The
matter was heard in April 2024 and later on August 21, 2024. We have received the closure order on December 20, 2024 in the favor of
the company and the refund of base amount of INR 17.4 million along with the applicable interest thereon of INR 7.99m dated July 08 2025.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">The
Department has filed an appeal before the Punjab &amp; Haryana High Court against the order of the CESTAT dated 20.12.2024. The matter
was listed before a Division Bench of the High Court on 19.01.2026. The High Court has issued notice only on the Application for delay
in filing the appeal and the application for delay in re-filing of the Appeal after curing defects. The matter was listed on 26.02.2026
but was not taken up on that date. It was again listed on 13.07.2026.However the matter was not taken up on 13.07.2026 the matter has
now been kept for hearing on 08.10.2026.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><span style="text-decoration: underline">Service
tax refund</span></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">Refund
claim of INR 2.54 million was filed in June 2018 and in response to the refund claim, a deficiency memo was issued by Assistant Commissioner,
GST, Gurugram on August 8, 2018 asking for certain information. TSI Yatra submitted requisite information vide reply dated January 23,
2019.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>


<!-- Field: Page; Sequence: 82; Value: 1 -->
    <div style="border-bottom: Black 1pt solid; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 6pt"><table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; font-size: 10pt"><tr style="vertical-align: top; text-align: left"><td style="text-align: center; width: 100%"><!-- Field: Sequence; Type: Arabic; Name: PageNo -->80<!-- Field: /Sequence --></td></tr></table></div>
    <div style="break-before: page; margin-top: 6pt; margin-bottom: 0pt"><table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; font-size: 10pt"><tr style="vertical-align: top; text-align: left"><td style="width: 100%"><a href="#Toc_001">Table of Contents</a></td></tr></table></div>
    <!-- Field: /Page -->

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">However
refund claim was rejected on the grounds of non-submission of information within a reasonable time from the date of issuance of deficiency
memo. This rejection order was not received by TSI Yatra and only after multiple follow ups TSI Yatra was provided with the copy of it
in September 2020.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">Accordingly,
appeal was filed before Commissioner (Appeals) on November 2, 2020 and personal hearing was granted on December 09, 2020. TSI Yatra submitted
the additional information sought by the officer pursuant to such hearing.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">The
Commissioner (Appeals) vide order dated February 12, 2021 has remanded back the matter for verification. TSI Yatra through its authorized
representatives has now approached the original authority for verification process. The matter is yet to be closed.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><span style="text-decoration: underline">Goods
and Services Tax Show Cause and Demand Notice -Fiscal Year 2018-19</span></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">For
the fiscal year 2018-19, TSI Yatra Private Limited faced a multi-issue dispute in Haryana starting with a Show Cause Notice on December
26, 2023, alleging an initial demand of 36.8 million primarily due to GSTR-2A versus GSTR-3B mismatches. Following the company&#8217;s
reply on February 23, 2024, the department issued an order under Section 73 on April 25, 2024, determining an excess claim demand of
4.24 million based on non-submission of supplier certificates and allegations against a supplier. TSI Yatra filed an appeal on July 23,
2024, and recording the 4.24 million demand as a contingent liability.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><span style="text-decoration: underline">Goods
and Services Tax Show Cause and Demand Notice -Fiscal Year 2019-20</span></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">For
the fiscal year 2019-20, TSI Yatra Private Limited faced a demand of 0.12 million from the Haryana GST Department under Section 16(2)(c)
relating to supplier non-payment of output tax by Starcrest Service Private Limited. The appellate authority maintained the demand subject
to future tax recovery from the vendor, prompting TSI Yatra to pay the 0.12 million under protest via Form DRC-03 on March 22, 2025.
Following a hearing in Gurugram, the company received departmental approval in September 2025 for a waiver of interest and penalty, and
continues to record the 0.12 million demand as a contingent liability.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><span style="text-decoration: underline">Goods
and Services Tax Show Cause and Demand Notice -Fiscal Year 2017-18</span></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">For
the fiscal year 2017-18, TSI Yatra Private Limited received a Show Cause Notice on August 4, 2024, from the Haryana GST Department alleging
short-paid output tax in GSTR-3B. Although the company demonstrated that the tax liability of 1.75 million had been settled in December
2019 via Form DRC-03, the department issued an order in Form DRC-07 on January 14, 2025, dropping the tax demand but confirming an interest
liability of 0.63 million. After an application under the GST amnesty scheme was rejected on November 20, 2025, the company filed an
official appeal on February 26, 2026, and recorded the 0.63 million demand as a contingent liability.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><span style="text-decoration: underline">Goods
and Services Tax Show Cause Notice -Fiscal Year 2020-21</span></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">For
the fiscal year 2020-21, TSI Yatra Private Limited received an offline DRC-01A notice dated October 17, 2024, from the Punjab GST Department
alleging excess Input Tax Credit availment of 0.60 million between GSTR-3B and GSTR-2A. The company submitted a written reply on November
6, 2024, demonstrating that the credit pertained to FY 2019-20 and was validly claimed in FY 2020-21. With no subsequent Show Cause Notice
or order issued and the statutory period under Section 73 having expired on February 28, 2025, the proceeding is time-barred, and the
company has categorized the 0.60 million exposure as remote.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><span style="text-decoration: underline">Goods
and Services Tax Show Cause Notice -Fiscal Year 2024-25</span></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">For
the fiscal year 2024-25, TSI Yatra Private Limited received a scrutiny notice in Form ASMT-10 on December 18, 2024, from the Uttar Pradesh
GST Department regarding an Input Tax Credit discrepancy of 0.01 million. The company submitted its response on January 18, 2025, explaining
that the credit pertained to September 2024 and was properly claimed in October 2024. Confident that the clarification and supporting
documents satisfy statutory requirements, the company anticipates the notice will be dropped and has classified the exposure as remote.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>


