<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><span style="text-decoration: underline">Goods
and Services Tax Show Cause Notice -Fiscal Year 2024-25</span></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">For
the fiscal year 2024-25, TSI Yatra Private Limited received a scrutiny notice in Form ASMT-10 from the Uttar Pradesh GST Department concerning
an Input Tax Credit variance of 0.01 million for the month of November 2024. Due to technical limitations on the online GST portal preventing
direct response submission, There has been no further communication from the department since then and has categorized the potential
liability as remote.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><span style="text-decoration: underline">Goods
and Services Tax Show Cause Notice -Fiscal Year 2024-25</span></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">For
the fiscal year 2024-25, TSI Yatra Private Limited received a scrutiny notice in Form ASMT-10 from the Uttar Pradesh GST Department regarding
an excess Input Tax Credit claim of 0.01 million for December 2024. The company filed an official reply on March 28, 2025, clarifying
that the credit originated from prior tax periods and was validly claimed in December 2024. Expecting the notice to be dropped following
document review, the company has recorded the matter as a remote liability.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><span style="text-decoration: underline">Goods
and Services Tax Show Cause Notice -Fiscal Year 2024-25</span></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">For
the fiscal year 2024-25, TSI Yatra Private Limited received a scrutiny notice in Form ASMT-10 from the Uttar Pradesh GST Department regarding
an Input Tax Credit variance of 0.01 million for January 2025. The company filed its online response on April 10, 2025, clarifying that
the credit related to prior months (October through December 2024) and was legitimately claimed in January 2025. Given the validity of
the credit claim, the company expects the notice to be dropped and has categorized the exposure as remote.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><span style="text-decoration: underline">Goods
and Service Tax Show Cause Notice-Fiscal Years 2020-21</span></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">The
company received Show cause notice in November 2024 following ASMT-10 &amp; DRC-01A, from department of Goods and Service Tax, Karnataka,
raising a demand of tax Rs.0.93m, interest Rs.0.77m, and penalty Rs. 0.11m. The company filed its response on December 26, 2024, explaining
the differences in output tax and input tax and justifying that there was no requirement to reverse the ITC. A personal hearing was attended
by the consultant in February 2025. An additional reply was submitted along with Form DRC-03 on February 21, 2025, with a payment of
Rs.0.060m. Supporting documents were also furnished during hearing and in additional response. After submitting all documents, payments
and hearings, the matter was closed in April 2025 with nil demand.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><span style="text-decoration: underline">Goods
and Service Tax Show Cause Notice-Fiscal Years 2020-21</span></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">TSI
Yatra Private Limited received a Show Cause Notice for FY 2020-21 on November 28, 2024, from the Department of Goods and Service Tax,
Uttar Pradesh, seeking clarification regarding differences in credit notes and an alleged excess claim of Input Tax Credit (ITC). The
company filed its detailed response on December 28, 2024. Following a personal hearing and the submission of supporting records, the
Adjudicating Authority issued an order on February 22, 2025, raising a total demand of 0.07 million (comprising 0.03m in tax, 0.02m in
interest, and 0.02m in penalty). The company fully paid this demand on June 24, 2025, successfully bringing the matter to a complete
close.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><span style="text-decoration: underline">Goods
and Service Tax Show Cause Notice-Fiscal Years 2020-21</span></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">The
Department of Goods and Service Tax, Haryana, issued notices dated October 15, 2024, requesting clarification of variations in
output and input taxes, ineligible ITC claims, outstanding trade payables, and other income details. TSI Yatra Private Limited
submitted its formal reply on December 27, 2024, along with relevant details, and attended 7 to 8 personal hearings to deliberate
the points with the tax officer. After evaluating the submissions, the Adjudicating Authority dropped several points and issued a
final demand order on February 26, 2025, for 0.59 million. The company discharged this demand in full on June 27, 2025 and received
the Nil demand order in 30 Jun 2025, thereby concluding the proceedings with no further liability pending.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>


