<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><span style="text-decoration: underline">Goods
and Services Tax Show Cause and Demand Notice -Fiscal Year 2017-18 to 2020-21</span></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">For
the fiscal years 2017-18 through 2020-21 (up to December 2020), Yatra for Business Private Limited faced an input tax credit reconciliation
dispute with the Superintendent of Central Tax, Preventive Section, Karnataka South Commissionerate. Following statement recording on
September 13, 2021, the company voluntarily deposited 10.92 million on September 26, 2021, covering tax liability and applicable interest.
However, the department issued a Show Cause Notice under Section 74 of the CGST Act on September 29, 2022, demanding a 25% penalty, and
subsequently issued an adverse order in Form DRC-07 creating a total demand of 11.7 million (comprising 5.16 million in interest and
6.58 million in penalty). The company filed an official appeal on April 28, 2025, contesting the time-barred invoking of Section 74,
and has recorded the 11.7 million demand as a contingent liability.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><span style="text-decoration: underline">Goods
and Services Tax Show Cause and Demand Notice -Fiscal Year 2017-18</span></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">For
the fiscal year 2017-18, Yatra for Business Private Limited received a scrutiny notice on September 13, 2022, from the Deputy Commissioner
of Central Goods and Service Tax, Division-III, Mumbai Central, alleging excess Input Tax Credit claimed in Form GSTR-3B compared to
Form GSTR-2A. Although the company paid the core tax liability of 11.6 million on November 29, 2022, and filed updated responses, the
department improperly invoked Section 74 instead of Section 73 and issued an adverse demand order totaling 24.1 million (comprising IGST
of 1.39 million, CGST of 11.4 million, and SGST of 11.4 million towards interest and penalty). The company subsequently filed an appeal
on May 1, 2025, and has classified the entire 24.1 million demand as a contingent liability. The appeal has been rejected by GST officer
in June 2026. Now the company is planning to file an appeal in GSTAT.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><span style="text-decoration: underline">Goods
and Services Tax Show Cause and Demand Notice -Fiscal Year 2020-21</span></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">For
the fiscal year 2020-21, Yatra for Business Private Limited received a notice dated September 7, 2022 (received September 13, 2022) from
the Deputy Commissioner of Central Goods and Service Tax, Division-III, Mumbai Central, alleging an Input Tax Credit mismatch between
GSTR-3B and GSTR-2A involving 3.43 million. The company filed an offline reply on November 14, 2022, clarifying that the actual discrepancy
was only 0.92 million stemming from an excess tax deposit adjustment. Because the department initiated no further action and the statutory
time limit for issuing an order under Section 73 lapsed on February 28, 2025, the notice is now time-barred, and the company has categorized
the liability as remote.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><span style="text-decoration: underline">Goods
and Services Tax A Show Cause and Demand Notice -Fiscal Year 2017-18</span></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">For
the fiscal year 2017-18, Yatra for Business Private Limited engaged in a dispute with the Department of Goods and Service Tax, Telangana,
originating from GSTR-1 and GSTR-3B mismatches. After receiving an order in Form DRC-07 on December 31, 2023, raising a final liability
of 0.53 million (excluding interest), the company accepted one issue and paid 0.13 million (via Form PMT-06). The company appealed the
remaining issues regarding late fees (which were already paid at the time of return filing) and output tax variance. With personal hearings
scheduled for April 8, 2026, the company has recorded 0.13 million as a provision and the remaining 0.40 million as a contingent liability.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><span style="text-decoration: underline">Goods
and Services Show Cause and Demand Notice -Fiscal Year 2017-18</span></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">For
the fiscal year 2017-18, Yatra for Business Private Limited received Show Cause Notice No. 13/2023-24 AC-DIV5 from the Bangalore Adjudicating
Authority concerning mismatches between GSTR-1, GSTR-3B, and GSTR-2A. Despite submitting comprehensive reconciliations and written responses,
the department issued an adverse order in Form DRC-07 raising a total demand of 16.6 million (split equally as 8.30 million in tax and
8.30 million in penalty) under Section 74. The company filed an appeal on May 1, 2025, contending that the notice was time-barred and
lacked grounds for fraud allegations, and has classified the 16.6 million demand as a contingent liability.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><span style="text-decoration: underline">Goods
and Services Tax Show Cause Notice -Fiscal Year 2020-21</span></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">For
the fiscal year 2020-21, Yatra for Business Private Limited received an offline ASMT-10 notice on September 25, 2024, from the Delhi
GST Department regarding output tax discrepancies (0.02 million) and Input Tax Credit claims (6.47 million). Following written
clarifications and submissions, the department issued Form DRC-01 on November 19, 2024, with a reduced demand of 6.47 million. The
company accepted the output tax liability of 0.02 million while providing Table 8A reconciliations for the remaining ITC. The
company has recorded 0.02 million as a provision and the remaining 6.47 million as a remote liability while awaiting final
departmental resolution.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>


