<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><span style="text-decoration: underline">Goods
and Services Tax Show Cause and Demand Notice -Fiscal Year 2017-18</span></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">For
the fiscal year 2017-18, Yatra for Business Private Limited faced an improper reopening of a settled matter by the Haryana GST Department,
which issued a fresh order in Form DRC-07 creating a demand of 5.01 million despite a favorable order having been passed on December
21, 2023. Because the fresh order was legally unsustainable and stemmed from a clerical error, the company filed an online rectification
application on November 4, 2025. Following multiple physical hearings before the adjudicating authority, the rectification order is currently
awaited, and the company has categorized the exposure as remote.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><span style="text-decoration: underline">Goods
and Service Tax Audit Notice-Fiscal Year 2021-22</span></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">For
the financial year 2021-22, Yatra for Business Private Limited underwent a TCS audit by the Department of Goods and Service Tax, Maharashtra.
Following initial documentation requests in June/July 2025 and an application to change the audit location, the department issued a notice
on August 29, 2025, highlighting discrepancies between the portal&#8217;s TCS details and the emailed data, raising an observation of
5.2 million. Following a personal hearing on September 4, 2025, detailed replies were submitted on September 6 and 8. The company filed
a DRC-03 for an accepted interest amount of 0.001 million under Para-6, and the officer dropped the remaining demand.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><span style="text-decoration: underline">Goods
and Service Tax Show Cause Notice-Fiscal Year 2021-22</span></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">For
the financial year 2021-22, Yatra for Business Private Limited was served an ASMT-10 notice on August 22, 2025, by the Department of
Goods and Service Tax, Tamil Nadu. The notice sought validation on whether credit notes shown in GSTR-1 were appropriately reversed by
recipients. A reply was submitted on September 20, 2025. The department later escalated the matter into a Show Cause Notice on September
25, 2025, adding a penalty. The company filed an adjournment request on October 9, 2025, and upon submitting the required documents concerning
nil-rated supplies and credit notes, the demand was successfully dropped.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><b><i>Tax
Matters Relating to Yatra Online Freight Services Private Limited</i></b></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 30pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -10pt"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><span style="text-decoration: underline">Assessment
Year 2022-23</span></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">The
Company filed its income tax return for Assessment Year (AY) 2022&#8211;23 declaring a loss of INR 106m. However, the assessment was
completed on a best judgment basis under Section 143(3) read with Section 144B of the Income-tax Act, 1961. An order dated 24th March
2024 was passed, assessing the income at &#8377;712.66 million and raising a demand of &#8377;236.49 million.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">The
primary reason for the addition of income was the non-reconciliation between turnover reported in the audited financial statements and
that reported on the GST portal. Aggrieved by the assessment order, the Company filed an appeal with CIT(A) on April 20, 2024.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">Further
submissions were made on December 18 2025 and the matter is yet to be disposed off.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><span style="text-decoration: underline">Assessment
Year 2024-25</span></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">The
case was selected for scrutiny under CASS. Accordingly, notice u/s 143(2) was issued on June 24 2025 and was duly served upon. The submission
of the company was perused and same was placed on record. Based on facts of case, material available on record and submission of the
company the income declared by the company in the return of income filed was accepted. Nil order was received by the company on February
26 2026.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>


