<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><b><i>Tax
Matters Relating to Globe All India Services Limited</i></b></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><span style="text-decoration: underline">Service
Tax matter</span></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">The
Company has received a service tax demand order amounting to INR 3.6 million (including penalty) pertaining to alleged non-disclosure
of taxable turnover and related discrepancies in ST-3 returns for the period from April 2016 to March 2017. The Order-in-Original dated
29 October 2024 was upheld by the Commissioner (Appeals) vide order dated 9 May 2024, against which the Company has filed a further appeal
before CESTAT, which is currently pending adjudication. As part of the appeal process, the Company has deposited the prescribed pre-deposit
amounts.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">The
matter primarily relates to factual issues concerning the reporting of turnover in ST-3 returns, including classification and
disclosure of turnover, and management believes that the relevant turnover has been appropriately accounted for in the books and the
related tax liability, where applicable, has been discharged. The Company is in a position to substantiate its contentions through
supporting records and documentation. Considering the status of the litigation, the nature of the issues involved, and the
uncertainty surrounding the ultimate outcome of the appeal, the company has disclosed this as contingent liability.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><span style="text-decoration: underline">Goods
and Service Tax Mumbai</span></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">The
Company received a GST demand of INR 8.3 million for FY 2019-20 arising primarily from differences between GSTR-1 and GSTR-3B,
mismatch relating to input tax credit, interest liability, and ITC reversal. The demand includes a tax component of INR 7.5 million
and penalty of INR .75 million. The Company has filed an appeal against the order and deposited the statutory pre-deposit amount of
INR .75 million, and the appeal remains pending adjudication.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">The
principal issue relates to a discrepancy between GSTR-1 and GSTR-3B returns, which arisen due to technical limitations in the GST portal
whereby credit notes exceeding the value of outward supplies could not be appropriately reflected in GSTR-3B, although the same were
duly disclosed in GSTR-1. Management believes that the underlying transactions have been correctly recorded and that the related tax
liability has been appropriately discharged. The Company has also provided supporting documentation to substantiate its position before
the appellate authorities.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">Considering
the factual nature of the matter, the documentation available, and the uncertainty associated with the outcome of the ongoing appellate
proceedings, the company has disclosed this as contingent liability.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><span style="text-decoration: underline">Goods
and Service Tax Delhi</span></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">The
Company has received a GST demand aggregating to INR 2.1 million. The demand primarily relates to (i) alleged short payment of tax due
to differences between GSTR-09/GSTR-01 and GSTR-3B, (ii) alleged availment of ineligible input tax credit, (iii) denial of input tax
credit pertaining to suppliers whose GST registrations were cancelled retrospectively, and (iv) consequential interest and penalty. The
Company has submitted its response and supporting documents before the authorities requesting withdrawal of the proceedings.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">The
principal component of the demand appears to arisen from reconciliation differences between annual return disclosures and liabilities
reported in GSTR-3B, including adjustments that could not be reflected in the manner alleged by the department. Management has represented
that the transactions have been appropriately recorded in the books of account and that no tax liability remains unpaid. Further, with
respect to the disputed input tax credit, management has stated that the credits relate to business purposes and has furnished supporting
documentation in support of its claim.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">While
certain aspects of the matter, particularly those relating to suppliers whose GST registrations were cancelled retrospectively, remain
dependent on verification of compliance by the respective suppliers, the Company believes that it has reasonable grounds to defend its
position. Accordingly, considering the nature of the issues involved, and the current stage of the proceedings, the company has disclosed this as contingent liability.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>


