<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><b><i>Revenue</i></b>.
We generated revenue of INR 7,954.5 million (USD 84.8 million) in the year ended March 31, 2025, an increase of 89.9% compared with 4,189.9
million (USD 44.7 million) in year ended March 31, 2024. Increase in revenue is mainly a combination of increase in our Hotels and Packages
business on account of our MICE business and full quarter impact of our recent acquisition of GAISL.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><b><i>Service
cost.</i></b> Our service cost increased to INR 4,039.0 million (USD 43.0 million) in the year ended March 31, 2025 from INR 866.0 million
(USD 9.2 million) in the year ended March 31, 2024 primarily on account of increase in our Hotels and Packages business due to MICE
business and full quarter impact of our recent acquisition of GAISL.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><b><i>Air
Ticketing.</i></b> Revenue from our Air Ticketing business was INR 1,925.3 million (USD 20.5 million) in the year ended March 31, 2025
against INR 1,729.3 million (USD 18.4 million) in the year ended March 31, 2024.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">Adjusted
Margin <sup>(1) </sup>from our Air Ticketing business decreased to INR 3,588.2 million (USD 38.2 million) in the year ended March 31,
2025 against INR 4,502.4 million (USD 48.0 million) in the year ended March 31, 2024. In the year ended March 31, 2025, Adjusted Margin
<sup>(1) </sup>for Air Ticketing includes the addition of INR 1,662.9 million (USD 17.7 million) in the year ended March 31, 2025 against
INR 2,773.1 million (USD 29.6 million) in the year ended March 31, 2024 of consumer promotion and loyalty program costs, which reduced
revenue as per IFRS 15. This decrease in Adjusted Margin is on account of decrease in air gross booking value by 20.3% and lower airline
incentive deals in the year ended March 31, 2025 as compared to year ended March 31, 2024.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><b><i>Hotels
and Packages.</i></b> Revenue from our Hotels and Packages business was INR 5,138.0 million (USD 54.8 million) in the year ended March
31, 2025 against INR 1,694.0 million (USD 18.1 million) in the year ended March 31, 2024.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">Adjusted
Margin <sup>(1)</sup> for this segment increased by 29.2% to INR 1,472.7 million (USD 15.7 million) in the year ended March 31, 2025
from INR 1,140.1 million (USD 12.2 million) in the year ended March 31, 2024. In the year ended March 31, 2025, Adjusted Margin <sup>(1)
</sup>for Hotels &amp; Packages includes the add-back of INR 350.7 million (USD 3.7 million) against INR 312.2 million (USD 3.3 million)
in the year ended March 31, 2024, of customer promotional expenses, which had been reduced from revenue as per IFRS 15. The increase
in adjusted margin is driven by increase in gross bookings of our Hotels and Packages business on account of MICE business and impact of our recent acquisition of GAISL.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><b>Other
Services<i>.</i></b> Our income from other services was INR 320.1 million (USD 3.4 million) in the year ended March 31, 2025, an increase
from INR 160.5 million (USD 1.7 million) in the year ended March 31, 2024. The increase in Adjusted Margin on account of recent acquisition of GAISL and increase in IT services revenue.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">Adjusted
Margin for this segment increased by 74.8% to INR 313.0 million (USD 3.3 million) in the year ended March 31, 2025 from INR 179.1 million
(USD 1.9 million) in the year ended March 31, 2024. In the year ended March 31, 2025, Adjusted Margin includes add-back of INR 15.9 million
(USD 0.2 million) in the year ended March 31, 2024 against INR 18.5 million (USD 0.2 million) in the year ended March 31, 2024 of consumer
promotion expenses, which had been reduced from revenue as per IFRS 15. The increase in Adjusted Margin on account of recent acquisition of GAISL
and increase in IT services revenue.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0"></p>

