<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 10pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -10pt"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><b>Off-Balance
Sheet Arrangements</b></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 10pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -10pt"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.25in">As of March 31,
2026, Group had obtained INR 200 million in bank guarantees from IDFC Bank, 50 million from Yes bank, and INR 100 million from
Federal bank against any payment default by us to all airlines participating in the International Air Transport Association&#8217;s
bill settlement plan. Further, during the fiscal year 2025-26, Yatra India along with its subsidiaries had provided bank guarantees
totaling INR 200 million for hotels and packages suppliers and for other business purposes.</p>
<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 10pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -10pt"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 10pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -10pt"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.25in"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">As
of March 31, 2025, Group had obtained INR 50 million in bank guarantees from IDFC Bank, 121 million from ICICI bank, against any
payment default by us to all airlines participating in the International Air Transport Association&#8217;s bill settlement plan. Further,
during the fiscal year 2024-25, Yatra India along with its subsidiaries had provided bank guarantees totaling INR 54.95 million for hotels
and packages suppliers and for other business purposes.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 10pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -10pt"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><b>&#160;</b></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.25in"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">As
of March 31, 2024, Group had obtained INR 50 million in bank guarantees from IDFC Bank and Yatra Freight had obtained INR 0.17
million in bank guarantees from ICICI Bank against any payment default by us to all airlines participating in the International Air Transport
Association&#8217;s bill settlement plan. Further, during the fiscal year 2023-24, Yatra India along with its subsidiaries had provided
bank guarantees totaling INR 56.95 million for hotels and packages suppliers and for other business purposes.</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 10pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -10pt"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><b>&#160;</b></span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0pt 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.25in"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">Apart
from the foregoing, we do not have any outstanding off-balance sheet derivative financial instruments, guarantees, interest rate swap
transactions or foreign currency forward contracts. We do not engage in trading activities involving non-exchange traded contracts.</span></p>

